<title>UK: IPAI annual alumina capacity includes new data.</title>
<headline>IPAI annual alumina capacity includes new data.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Annual alumina production capacity estimates by the International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) included data from China, Azerbaijan, Kazakhstan and Montenegro for the first time.</p>
<p>The IPAI said that at the end of the century world alumina production capacity will be 52.121 million tonnes compared with 50.225 million tonnes at the end of 1996.</p>
<p>Capacity at the end of June 1996, before the new data was included was 44.843 million tonnes, the IPAI data showed.</p>
<p>London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7771</p>
</text>
